<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">dollmaster-routes</ansi>

The Doll Master is a neutral lineage. At level 10 it promotes to one of three
classes, and any alignment may choose any of them. Each class adds four ranks
(10, 15, 20, 25); a talent adds more (<ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Puppeteer</ansi>

  10 Two dolls          a second doll, each at 50% of the doll health, so the
                        Master has two strikes a turn; Guard String works for
                        both dolls
  15 Practiced hands    +2 Attack on the dolls' blows
  20 Sturdier dolls     each doll has 60% of the doll health
  25 Lacquered dolls    +4 armor on each doll

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Golemancer</ansi>

  10 Golem              one golem in place of the doll: 130% of the doll
                        health and +15 armor, but it can't wear armor (its
                        body is its armor); Guard String 4 times a battle
  15 Heavy fists        +1 damage on the golem's blows
  20 Deep core          the golem has 150% of the doll health
  25 Stone skin         +25 armor on the golem

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Marionettist</ansi>

  10 Tangling strings   Tangle snags two foes and is ready after 2 rounds
                        instead of 3
  15 Practiced hands    +2 Attack on the doll's blows
  20 Hard pull          Tangle pushes a foe back 10 more meter points
  25 Fine carving       +2 damage on the doll's blows

The elite classes of these routes (Grand Puppeteer, Golem Lord, String
Sovereign) are still to come; until then a Doll Master keeps its advanced
class's ranks.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Talents</ansi>

Hardwood (+10% doll health), Stout Strings (Guard String one more time, once),
Fine Carving (+1 doll damage) and Steady Hand (+2 doll Attack) suit any route
(<ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>).

See also: <ansi fg="command">help dollmaster</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help doll</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help classes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help abilities</ansi>.
